18	## Color Palette
19	
20	```css
21	:root {
22	  /* --- BACKGROUNDS --- */
23	  --color-bg:             #FAF7F2;       /* warm off-white, like aged paper */
24	  --color-bg-warm:        #F5F0E8;       /* slightly warmer for alternating modules */
25	  --color-bg-code:        #1E1E2E;       /* deep indigo-charcoal for code blocks */
26	  --color-text:           #2C2A28;       /* dark charcoal, easy on eyes */
27	  --color-text-secondary: #6B6560;       /* warm gray for secondary text */
28	  --color-text-muted:     #9E9790;       /* muted for timestamps, labels */
29	  --color-border:         #E5DFD6;       /* subtle warm border */
30	  --color-border-light:   #EEEBE5;       /* even lighter border */
31	  --color-surface:        #FFFFFF;       /* card surfaces */
32	  --color-surface-warm:   #FDF9F3;       /* warm card surface */
33	
34	  /* --- ACCENT (adapt per project — pick ONE bold color) ---
35	     Default: vermillion. Alternatives: coral (#E06B56), teal (#2A7B9B),
36	     amber (#D4A843), forest (#2D8B55). Avoid purple gradients. */
37	  --color-accent:         #D94F30;
38	  --color-accent-hover:   #C4432A;
39	  --color-accent-light:   #FDEEE9;
40	  --color-accent-muted:   #E8836C;
41	
42	  /* --- SEMANTIC --- */
43	  --color-success:        #2D8B55;
44	  --color-success-light:  #E8F5EE;
45	  --color-error:          #C93B3B;
46	  --color-error-light:    #FDE8E8;
47	  --color-info:           #2A7B9B;
48	  --color-info-light:     #E4F2F7;
49	
50	  /* --- ACTOR COLORS (assign to main components) ---
51	     Each major "character" in the codebase gets a distinct color
52	     for chat bubbles, diagrams, and highlights */
53	  --color-actor-1:        #D94F30;       /* vermillion */
54	  --color-actor-2:        #2A7B9B;       /* teal */
55	  --color-actor-3:        #7B6DAA;       /* muted plum */
56	  --color-actor-4:        #D4A843;       /* golden */
57	  --color-actor-5:        #2D8B55;       /* forest */
58	}
59	```
60	
61	**Rules:**
62	- Even-numbered modules use `--color-bg`, odd-numbered use `--color-bg-warm` (alternating backgrounds create visual rhythm)
63	- Actor colors should be visually distinct from each other and from the accent
64	- Code blocks always use `--color-bg-code` with light text
