232	## Navigation & Progress
233	
234	**HTML structure:**
235	```html
236	<nav class="nav">
237	  <div class="progress-bar" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="0"></div>
238	  <div class="nav-inner">
239	    <span class="nav-title">Course Title</span>
240	    <div class="nav-dots">
241	      <button class="nav-dot" data-target="module-1" data-tooltip="Module 1 Name"
242	              role="tab" aria-label="Module 1"></button>
243	      <!-- one per module -->
244	    </div>
245	  </div>
246	</nav>
247	```
248	
249	**Progress bar (CSS-only where possible, JS fallback):**
250	```javascript
251	function updateProgressBar() {
252	  const scrollTop = window.scrollY;
253	  const scrollHeight = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
254	  const progress = (scrollTop / scrollHeight) * 100;
255	  progressBar.style.width = progress + '%';
256	}
257	window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
258	  requestAnimationFrame(updateProgressBar);
259	}, { passive: true });
260	```
261	
262	**Nav dot states:**
263	- Default: `border: 2px solid var(--color-text-muted)`, empty center
264	- Current: `border-color: var(--color-accent)`, filled center, subtle glow shadow
265	- Visited: `background: var(--color-accent)`, filled solid
266	
267	**Keyboard navigation:**
268	```javascript
269	document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
270	  if (['INPUT', 'TEXTAREA'].includes(e.target.tagName)) return;
271	  if (e.key === 'ArrowDown' || e.key === 'ArrowRight') { nextModule(); e.preventDefault(); }
272	  if (e.key === 'ArrowUp' || e.key === 'ArrowLeft') { prevModule(); e.preventDefault(); }
273	});
274	```
