367	## Code Block Globals
368	
369	All code blocks in the course — whether inside translation blocks, standalone snippets, or quiz challenges — must wrap text and never show a horizontal scrollbar. This is a teaching tool, not an IDE.
370	
371	```css
372	pre, code {
373	  white-space: pre-wrap;       /* wrap long lines */
374	  word-break: break-word;      /* break mid-word if absolutely needed */
375	  overflow-x: hidden;          /* no horizontal scrollbar — ever */
376	}
377	/* Hide scrollbars on code containers */
378	.translation-code::-webkit-scrollbar,
379	pre::-webkit-scrollbar {
380	  display: none;
381	}
382	```
383	
384	Code snippets must be **exact copies** from the real codebase — never modified, trimmed, or simplified. Instead, choose naturally short (5-10 line) sections from the code that illustrate the concept well. If a longer block is needed, show it all — the wrapping CSS will handle readability.
